  "title": "Vertex AI: LoRA & Super Res for Video, Agent Model Config",
  "summary": "Vertex AI's v1beta1 API now offers powerful new capabilities for video generation, including LoRA for stylization and Pro Super Res upsampling. Agents gain more control with default model configurations, and evaluation runs can now utilize cross-region models.",
  "details": "Developers can now fine-tune video generation experiments using `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperiments`. This includes the new `loraConfig` for applying LoRA adapters for Omni editing/stylization, and `superResConfig` for Pro Super Res upsampling with modes like `MODE_4K` and `MODE_8K`. For agents, the `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Agent` resource now supports an optional `modelConfig` field, allowing you to set default `model` and `temperature` parameters for an agent's generation tasks. Additionally, `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScope` introduces `autoEnroll` for easier agent monitoring. Evaluation workflows are enhanced with `allowCrossRegionModel` in `EvaluateInstancesRequest` and `EvaluationRunEvaluationConfig`, providing more flexibility. Granular control over automated evaluation metrics is also available via `stepAutoraterConfigs` in `PredefinedMetricSpec`. Note that `temperature` and `topP` fields in `GenaiVertexV1beta1GenerationConfig` have been deprecated; developers should update their usage accordingly.",
